SUMMARY="Node.js JavaScript runtime for Haiku ARM64"
DESCRIPTION="Native Node.js 24.21.0 runtime for Haiku ARM64, built from upstream source \
directly on a Haiku arm64 VM, not cross-built in the haiku-builder container like \
golang_bin or fastfetch -- Node's own build (gyp/ninja, plus running the freshly built \
node_mksnapshot on the target itself to generate the V8 startup snapshot) needs to run \
natively, not just cross-compile. Bundles libuv, libbrotlicommon/dec/enc and \
libcares/libnghttp2 runtimes, since those are not separately on this repository and/or \
not at the version this Node needs; openssl3, icu74 and zlib are left to the base \
system, which already provides them (confirmed present under /boot/system/lib on the \
RENKU arm64 image). Revision 2 fixes two issues found stress-testing a real Next.js app \
over SSH, the only way most users reach this package: (1) this image's icu74 is a \
bootstrap-only stub, with the real ICU data file at /boot/system/data/icu/74.1 -- only \
the desktop launch target's SetupEnvironment set ICU_DATA to it, so any Intl use (new \
Intl.DateTimeFormat, npm's own string-locale-compare) crashed or threw under sshd; bin/node \
is now a wrapper that sets ICU_DATA before exec'ing the real binary, which moved to \
bin/node-real. (2) npm/npx were never wired up (node_install_npm was false); bin/npm and \
bin/npx are now wrapper scripts over a packaged copy of Node's own bundled npm CLI \
(deps/npm, minus its test/docs/man trees), staged at lib/node/npm. Next.js note (supersedes \
an earlier, incorrect caveat here blaming the WASM SWC fallback itself): next-swc has no \
haiku/arm64 native build, but Next.js's WASM fallback (auto-downloaded from \
@next/swc-wasm-nodejs on the first 'next build', landing itself at the exact \
node_modules/next/wasm/@next/swc-wasm-nodejs path its own loader expects, no npm/PATH \
issue once this package's npm/npx wrappers are installed) works correctly and needs no \
manual file placement -- confirmed by instrumenting next/dist/build/swc/index.js directly: \
every SWC transform call during a real build succeeds (isWasm=true, valid output) across \
100+ modules. The actual failure some users hit ('next build' erroring with \"'import' and \
'export' may appear only with sourceType: module\" on every app/*.js file) is unrelated to \
this package, to SWC, or to WASM: it is triggered by 'npm init -y' (this npm 11 CLI's \
default behavior) writing an explicit \"type\": \"commonjs\" into package.json, which \
Next.js 15's webpack config handles differently from a package.json with no \"type\" field \
at all (the common case for most real Next.js projects, including ones scaffolded with \
create-next-app) -- with the explicit field present, webpack parses the SWC-transformed \
app-router output with the wrong sourceType and the build fails; remove that field (or never \
add it) and the exact same WASM-backed build succeeds. Confirmed end to end twice, from \
'npm init -y' through a real HTTP 200 from curl against 'next start', by deleting the \
\"type\" field from package.json before building -- no SWC/WASM file placement, postinstall \
hook, or nodejs_bin change needed."
HOMEPAGE="https://nodejs.org/"
VERSION="24.21.0"
REVISION="2"
LICENSE="MIT"
COPYRIGHT="2009-2026 Node.js contributors"
ARCHITECTURES_SUPPORTED="arm64"

PROVIDES="nodejs_bin = $VERSION
cmd:node = $VERSION
cmd:npm = $VERSION
cmd:npx = $VERSION"
REQUIRES="haiku"

NOTE="built natively on a Haiku arm64 VM, not cross-built: see scripts/cross-arm64-libuv.sh \
for the one real dependency fix this needed (a pre-staged libuv was a version behind what \
this Node release requires, missing uv_thread_setname entirely -- rebuilt from Node's own \
bundled deps/uv source for an exact version match). The other three bundled runtimes (brotli, \
c-ares, nghttp2) now also have their own cross-build scripts -- cross-arm64-brotli.sh, \
cross-arm64-cares.sh, cross-arm64-nghttp2.sh, written and verified after the fact against \
node v24.21.0's actual vendored deps/ sources; building from scratch with them gives \
libbrotli{common,dec,enc}.so.1.2.0 and libcares.so.2.19.7, one patch version ahead of what \
this package's own staged libs (1.1.0, 2.19.3) actually are -- SONAME-compatible either way, \
and the staged versions are what this package was actually built and tested against, but \
prefer the scripts' output on a future rebuild. libnghttp2 matches exactly (14.29.5). \
scripts/build-nodejs-native.sh orchestrates the whole thing -- the four library cross-builds \
above (run inside haiku-builder), then this script's own native ./configure && make, then \
scripts/stage-nodejs-package.sh -- though running all of it back to back on one from-scratch \
checkout has not itself been done; each piece was verified separately (see each script's own \
header). The .hpkg under prebuilt/arm64/ was produced by staging out/Release/node (stripped) \
plus the four bundled .so runtimes above, packaged and install-tested with the target's own \
native package/pkgman tools. Revision 2 \
renames the real binary to bin/node-real and adds bin/node/bin/npm/bin/npx wrapper scripts \
(export ICU_DATA=/boot/system/data/icu/74.1, exec the real binary) plus a packaged copy of \
Node's own bundled npm CLI (deps/npm, test/docs/man excluded) staged at lib/node/npm -- \
fixing Intl crashes and the missing npm/npx under SSH sessions, found stress-testing a real \
Next.js 15.1.6 app end to end."

PREBUILT_PACKAGES="pkgman-repo/prebuilt/arm64/nodejs_bin-$VERSION-$REVISION-arm64.hpkg"
